2026-10-30T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2348) 'One workspace checkout holds both the taskweft rows and this workspace's own.
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2348  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2348) 'The taskweft workspace and this one were two clients of two manifests. Work that needed both had no single checkout.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2348  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2348) 'Read below for the checks that passed and the work still open.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2348  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2348) 'What was decided, how it was checked, and what is still open
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2348  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2348) 'The workspace manifest is a superset of the taskweft manifest, by path. Where both place a path, this workspace's row wins, so rung pins never move through the merge. Every other taskweft row is added with `groups="notdefault,taskweft"`, pinned to the commit its branch or tag had on the day it was added, with `upstream` naming that ref. The bootstrap runs `repo init -g default,taskweft`, so a new workspace syncs both sets. A plain `repo init` still syncs the workspace's own rows only.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2348  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2348) '- RFD66606-2346, the last change that added manifest rows; RFD66606-2341, dev.next.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2348  1 LINE
 Text:Written

