 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2348  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2348) 'The operator's decisions
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2348  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2348) '1. The taskweft rows the blocklist names (the OpenBao service and the Bao on SQLite and FoundationDB service) and `iceoryx2` are added as they are. They are placed for study. No workspace repo depends on them.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2348  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2348) '2. New rows are pinned to a commit, as every upstream row here is.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2348  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2348) '3. The rows are an opt-in group. The bootstrap opts in. `WEFTSPUN_GROUPS=default` gives the workspace's own rows alone.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2348  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2348) 'Why a plain copy fails
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2348  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2348) 'Taskweft rows track branches and include rows this org blocks, so a plain copy would have broken the pin rule and put blocked repos in every default sync.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2348  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2348) 'The merge rules
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2348  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2348) 'The comparison is by path, because a path is what `repo` collides on. 11 paths are in both manifests. At the bootstrap path the two rows name different repos, and the private fork stays. The datasource store keeps this workspace's row, so taskweft's two linkfiles into the Bao on SQLite and FoundationDB service are not placed. GitHub rows use the one `origin` remote with an org-qualified name. The nine Hugging Face rows need two absolute remotes, `huggingface` and `huggingface-datasets`.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2348  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2348) 'Numbers and checks
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2348  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2348) 'taskweft had 180 rows: 169 added, 21 of them already pinned by commit. The manifest went from 20 to 189 rows. Every branch and tag resolved with `git ls-remote`, with 0 failures. The four manifest gates passed locally, each after its self-test, and the five CI jobs passed on the pull request and on `main` after the merge. A scratch `repo init` listed 189 rows with the group and 20 with `-g default`, which is the control. `repo list` without `-a` shows 0 rows before a sync, so it proves nothing about a fresh client.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2348  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2348) 'Still open
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2348  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2348) 'Nothing keeps the superset true as taskweft moves: a new taskweft row is absent here until someone adds it. The bootstrap repo's workflow is active but has never run, and this repo has no workflow, so neither change was checked in CI. No `pwsh` was available, so the PowerShell change was not parsed. The private org is invisible to the `gh` wrapper; its pull requests go through the REST API with a `bao-mint-github` token, which prints the token and its expiry on one line.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2348  1 LINE
 Text:Written
